<title>USA: Chris-Craft Industries Inc Q1 net rises.</title>
<headline>Chris-Craft Industries Inc Q1 net rises.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Condensed Consolidated Statements of Income</p>
<p>		   Three Months Ended March 31, 1997 and 1996</p>
<p>		(Unaudited - In thousands except per share data)</p>
<p>						    1997	    1996</p>
<p> Operating revenues		   $   106,472   $   105,650</p>
<p> Operating income			    17,525	  17,873</p>
<p>Other income (expense):</p>
<p>Gain on change of ownership</p>
<p>     in UPN, net			    152,224		--</p>
<p>   Interest and other income, net	19,285	  23,160</p>
<p>Equity in United Paramount</p>
<p>     Network loss (a)		    (17,898)	(32,754)</p>
<p>						  153,611	 (9,594)</p>
<p>Income before income taxes</p>
<p>    and minority interest		 171,136	   8,279</p>
<p> Income tax provision			68,500	   4,100</p>
<p>Income before minority</p>
<p>     interest				 102,636	   4,179</p>
<p> Minority interest (b)		   (27,477)	 (3,804)</p>
<p>   Net income (c)			    75,159	     375</p>
<p>Average common equivalent  </p>
<p>   shares outstanding (d)		  31,867	  31,388</p>
<p>Net income per share (d):</p>
<p>   Primary					 2.36	     .01</p>
<p> Fully diluted				   1.88	     .01</p>
<p>(a) BHC Communications Inc, Chris-Craft's television broadcasting subsidiary, owned 100 percent of UPN from UPN's 1994 inception through January 15, 1997, when Viacom Inc completed the exercise of its option to acquire a 50 percent interest in UPN. BHC and Viacom now share equally in UPN's losses and funding requirements.  BHC continues to account for its interest in UPN under the equity method.</p>
<p>(b)  Reflects the interest of stockholders other than Chris-Craft in the operating results of BHC, 76 percent owned at March 31, 1997, and the interest of stockholders other than BHC in the operating results of United Television Inc, 59 percent owned by BHC at March 31, 1997.</p>
<p>(c)  Before preferred stock dividend requirements of $105 in 1997 and $114 in 1996.</p>
<p>(d)  After giving effect to the April 1997 3% stock dividend.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610</p>
